  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Rainbow. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Rainbow is a vibrant, strategic card game that focuses on completing a spectrum of colors while avoiding 'Clouds'. Players place cards into a shared central line to build a six-color rainbow. It is a game of careful hand management and risk assessment: if you add a duplicate color or a cloud card to the line, you are forced to collect all the cards currently on the table (which is bad for scoring). The winner is the player who collects the most 'Natural' rainbows or the fewest penalty cards, depending on the variant.",
    objective: 'Complete 6-color rainbows to collect cards, or have the most cards at the end.',
    gameplay: 'On your turn you play one card from your hand to the central Rainbow Line. The line builds toward a set of six different colors. If you play a card whose color is already in the line, or play a Cloud card, you must collect all cards currently in the line into your penalty pile. Wild cards can represent any color. The goal is to complete full rainbows to collect cards for points while minimizing penalty collections.',
    keyRules: [
      'Play one card per turn to the central Rainbow Line.',
      'Duplicate color or a Cloud in the line forces you to collect all cards from the line as a penalty.',
      'Complete six different colors in the line to form a Natural rainbow and collect those cards.',
      'Wild cards count as any color; hold Wilds for the 5th or 6th slot when possible.',
      'Winner has the most Natural rainbows or fewest penalty cards depending on variant.',
    ],
